A||||20||BAM-BAM||Got cooked by a ricer....Dam!!||||1||
Z||000000||BAM-BAM||05-06-2000||09:10 PM||||  What the... I was on my way home from work today when this chico in a green Honda Accord EX (station wagon) rolls up and keeps pace. I push ahead, not really wanting to have a go but rather, get rid of that annoying fart pipe. Anyway, we catch a light and he pulls up to the line. I creep up a little and he creeps up with that dragster style jerking motion. Light turns green, I throw the auto into #1 untill I hit about 4500 bounce into #2 just in time to see a green blurr pass me on the right. I shut it down right at 50MPH as he continues on. Now I'm not a racer and do not condone that kind of sport on the streets. This was one of those rare instances where we were in a rather rural area on a diveded two way thouroughfare (no children present). I have an 85GT auto, the only mod is an ADS Superchip, 105k miles. The care runs great. So, what happened? I'm thinking these cars should be able to at least outrun a Honda station wagon. Now more than ever, I am convinced that the 3.4HO is in my future. I do not like being the underdog in that way.<BR>So, if anyone has any suggestions or solutions, please, feel free to pitch in.<BR>Thanks for letting me vent.<P> BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  ||||reg||1
Z||000001||2birds||05-06-2000||10:36 PM||||Another victim of the sleeper Honda.  I feel your pain.  Our little 135+ HP V-6's are no match for an Acura Integra engine (no-brainer swap for 200 unmodified HP in an accord or civic).  I see a lot of intercoolers hidden (not so well) under the front ends of a lot of accords and civics around here, and I stay clear.  Apparently bagging groceries pays better than it did when I was in high school, and all we could afford were nasty old V-8 powered American muscle cars.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Hock||05-06-2000||11:13 PM||||YOU KNOW, THAT WOULD P@#S ME OFF!! DID YOU EVER THINK OF A SHIFT KIT? I KNOW THOSE AUTOS SHIFT KINDA SLOW OR HOW ABOUT A SET OF UNDER DRIVE PULLEYS. MAYBE EVEN UNCORKING YOUR EXHAUST SYSTEM MIGHT HELP. <P>AHH, F@#% IT!! GET A DAMN TURBO AND SOME NOS. I PROMISE YOU THE ONLY THING YOU'LL LOSE TO THEN IS A TOP FUEL DRAGSTER, AND IF YOU SEE ONE OF THOSE ON THE STREET BE SURE AND LET US KNOW ABOUT IT.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cooter||05-06-2000||11:37 PM||||Some of those EX cars have the vtec 4 banger and even a few rolled off the line with an acura looking v6. The v6 cars have "duals" out the back bumper and are pretty quick, even for a station wagon! Damn I hate getting out run by station wagons.||||reg||1
Z||000004||RobertVol||05-07-2000||02:35 AM||||Yeah 2birds there is alot of those around. There is a total stock looking white honda accord in OP with 240 horses. Had turbo from Chassis Craft on Blanding put it in..Man that thing will scream. They wanted to put a turbonetic-4 in mine and do a bunch of mods but when they gave me the price for this "LITTLE" project it was like $6,000 ..I said uh hmmm NO!||||reg||1
Z||000005||Phaeton||05-07-2000||05:10 AM||||I own my Fiero for handling, straightline acceleration has different priorities.<P>Perhaps I am just fortunate to have a twenty mile "chase" road winding along the north bank of the Tanana River.  I drive out and back regular all summer, pushing it just for the exhilaration.<P>No autocross operating in the area or would be racing with them.||||reg||12
Z||000006||Fformula88||05-07-2000||10:55 AM||||Bagging groceries can make you a ton of money if... 1.) you work 60 hrs a week, 2.) you never go out and forgoe having a life 3.) you spend all of your extra cash on Honda bolt on parts.<P>I know they love their fast, modded honda's, but I'd rather have a Fiero with ANY engine than be forced to drive around in a Honda.  It just looks way cooler!||||reg||10
