Z||000012||Dan86gt3.8||05-08-2000||11:16 AM||||Glad to hear you are happy with ace.  Everbody I talked to after I did it only had bad things to say about him.  I thinks its a great conversion, me and my dad did the kit at home.  My only compliant is he took forever to get us our stuff.  But ya I toast most of the ricers I come across (haven't run across any of the talons running 25 psi's of boost yet).  I have also beat some auto 5.0 stang's.  they are usually the ones that are pissed.  I am trying to get the word out that the 3.8 is defenitely the way to go.  I would be talking crazy s#!t if I had the supercharged version.  Hey have you raced any of the new f-bods or vettes with the ls1 yet?  Are you running stock boost or did you up it with the afdtermarket pulley?  And did ace do it in colarado or did you do it at home with a kit?||||reg||1
Z||000013||RobertVol||05-08-2000||11:23 PM||||Hey Stimpy ! I am to so you can say it..You have my permmision Awl 'right ? <P>And yeah Dan I love smoking 5.0's. <BR>I am running stock GEN II SC the 240 HP engine. This was an ordered engine for a 99 Buick Grans sport that had a problem. They ordered the engine but then did not use it. So i got a great deal. The engine SCREAms. And yes I can hang and sometimes beat LS'1 from light to light. depending on the driver. This is a REAL sub 6 sec 0-60 car. I woould say on average 5.8 - 6.2 times. Havnt tried a COrvette and dont think I want to. Around here though most people that can afford a NEW vette dont really like to RUN them. I took mune to CO to get it done. nobody could do it here ....||||reg||1
